CMHC conducts its Rental Market Survey every year in October. It collects data from a sample of landlords and property managers, and CMHC publishes the results in the Rental Market Report, usually in December.

**Structures covered:** The survey covers privately initiated, purpose-built rental structures in urban centres with a population of 10,000 or more. It includes:
- Row (townhouse) structures with 3 or more units.
- Apartment structures with 3 or more units.

The survey does not cover secondary rental market units such as rented condominiums, single-detached houses, duplexes, accessory apartments and other non-purpose-built rentals. CMHC reports on those separately in its Secondary Rental Market Survey. I did not check CMHC's current methodology page with a tool, so this comes from my own knowledge of the survey. Confirm the details, such as the minimum structure size, on CMHC's Rental Market Survey methodology page.

